{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>By signs.</b> There were signs on each and every banner. Our predecessors said that on the banner of Reuben was the figure of a man, by force of the derash of duda'im, and on the banner of Judah the figure of a lion, for thus Jacob likened him, and on the banner of Ephraim the figure of an ox, on account of 'firstborn bull,' and on the banner of Dan the figure of an eagle, so that they resembled the cherubim that Ezekiel the prophet saw." "<b>Opposite.</b> Distant."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:57.335074540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}